What is Matplotlib?

Matplotlib is a Python library used to create:

Line Charts
Bar Charts
Pie Charts
Histograms
Scatter Plots
Subplots
Data Visualization


pip3 install matplotlib

Import:

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

-----------


1. Line Chart

Used to show trends over time.


import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
y = [10, 20, 15, 25, 30]

plt.plot(x, y)

plt.title("Sales Trend")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")

plt.show()


----


Output:

A line connecting all points.


---------


2. Bar Chart

Used to compare categories.



import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

subjects = ["Math", "Science", "English"]
marks = [85, 90, 75]

plt.bar(subjects, marks)

plt.title("Student Marks")
plt.xlabel("Subjects")
plt.ylabel("Marks")

plt.show()



------------


3. Pie Chart

Used to show percentages.

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

sizes = [40, 30, 20, 10]

labels = ["IT", "HR", "Finance", "Sales"]

plt.pie(sizes, labels=labels, autopct="%1.1f%%")

plt.show()



Output:


Circular pie chart



-------------



4. Histogram

Shows data distribution.



.py

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

marks = [85, 90, 45, 70, 35, 95, 60]

plt.hist(marks)

plt.title("Marks Distribution")
plt.xlabel("Marks")
plt.ylabel("Students")

plt.show()

-------------


5. Scatter Plot

Shows relationship between two variables.



import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

height = [150, 160, 170, 180, 190]
weight = [50, 60, 70, 80, 90]

plt.scatter(height, weight)

plt.xlabel("Height")
plt.ylabel("Weight")

plt.show()



